{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the booty, etc., and the half was, etc., and the levy was, etc., and the half-portion of, etc.</b> One needs to know why He elaborated so at length in the details of the reckoning regarding something that anyone who comes to count can know that thus the half amounts to such and thus the levy amounts to such, etc. Also regarding the matter of the congregation's half-portion He did not elaborate to state all the details of the sums but only the reckoning that results from half the booty — and regarding this too I would say that there was no need to state it. And the Ramban, upon him be peace, wrote the reason for the matter: that He came to inform us that not one was missing from the time of the [initial] number to the time when it was halved — end quote. And this does not seem right in my eyes, for the fact that nothing was lost from the livestock in a short amount of time — in that there is a miracle — and all the more so that the verse should need to write all these things for its sake." "<b>But what seems correct</b> in my eyes is this: that the specification of the reckoning's details for the half-portion of those who went out in the army is to reveal that the levy was counted from within it — not that they would count five hundred and give one to HaShem from the levy's portion, but rather they counted four hundred ninety-nine and gave one. Therefore He brought up all the details of the levy's reckoning, and from it you will know that they gave one per four hundred ninety-nine." "And the specification of the reckoning of the congregation's half-portion — the verse comes to remove another error, namely that a person might say: the levy given by the men of the army was always one out of five hundred from without [i.e., from the full count], and there is no proof from the sum of the levy, for one could say that the levy resulting from the levy [calculation] would not have amounted to the levy of three hundred thirty-seven thousand five hundred sheep for the stated number [if taken from the soldiers' half alone]. One could say that they gave that levy from the congregation's half-portion — for by this means the stated number would result in the levy of the army's portion even if it were given from without [i.e., from the full count]. Therefore the verse came and counted the number of the congregation's portion and counted it whole, to remove this concern. And for this reason the verse did not detail the number of the congregation's portion but only the half's number, for the purpose of what I have written — that the levy was given from within it and each one paid his share from his half. And this too is what HaShem commanded him in the statement ״מִמַּחֲצִיתָם תִּקָּחוּ״ — to say that they should not exact the levy except from their half. And He also said ״אֶחָד מִחֲמֵשׁ מֵאוֹת״ — you thus learn that the levy must be מִלְּגָיו [from within the half-count]."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:23.292726228Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}